{
  "_comment": [
    "Ensemble scenario configuration for the EA-EM pipeline (run_pipeline.py).",
    "Each top-level key (except '_comment' and '_schema') is a named scenario.",
    "Pass the scenario name via:  python run_pipeline.py --scenario <name>",
    "The special name 'default' is used when no --scenario flag is given.",
    "════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════",
    "FIELD REFERENCE",
    "════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════",
    "output_dir        str   Output folder for plots, cache, and NPY files.",
    "                        Example: \"output_dir\": \"mfc2_outputs/my_run\"",
    "realization_index int   Which synthetic ground-truth member to use (0-based).",
    "                        Ignored when using real field data.",
    "                        Example: \"realization_index\": 0",
    "depths0           list  Starting layer interface depths [m], length = n_layers-1.",
    "                        Always required; defines the number of layers.",
    "                        Examples:",
    "                          3-layer soil (0–0.3, 0.3–0.6, 0.6–1.0 m):",
    "                            \"depths0\": [0.3, 0.6, 1.0]",
    "                          5-layer high-resolution profile:",
    "                            \"depths0\": [0.2, 0.4, 0.7, 1.1]",
    "fixed_depths      bool  True  → all interfaces pinned (classic mode).",
    "              or  list  False → all interfaces free to move during inversion.",
    "                        [bool…] → per-interface control, same length as depths0.",
    "                        Examples:",
    "                          All fixed:   \"fixed_depths\": true",
    "                          All free:    \"fixed_depths\": false",
    "                          Mixed (pin top and bottom, free middle):",
    "                            \"fixed_depths\": [true, false, true]",
    "                          Mixed (pin top only, free deeper interfaces):",
    "                            \"fixed_depths\": [true, false, false]",
    "param_grid        obj   Cartesian-product inversion parameter sweep.",
    "                        Every combination of values becomes one ensemble member.",
    "                        Recognised keys (all optional, all accept a list):",
    "                          alpha        regularisation weight  (float > 0)",
    "                          method       scipy optimiser string",
    "                          forwardModel EMagPy forward model key",
    "                        Examples:",
    "                          Minimal single-member sweep:",
    "                            \"param_grid\": {",
    "                              \"alpha\": [0.03],",
    "                              \"method\": [\"L-BFGS-B\"],",
    "                              \"forwardModel\": [\"FSlin\"]",
    "                            }",
    "                          8-member sweep (2 alpha × 2 method × 2 model):",
    "                            \"param_grid\": {",
    "                              \"alpha\": [0.03, 0.20],",
    "                              \"method\": [\"L-BFGS-B\", \"CG\"],",
    "                              \"forwardModel\": [\"FSlin\", \"CS\"]",
    "                            }",
    "                          Valid method values:  L-BFGS-B | CG | Nelder-Mead | SLSQP | TNC",
    "                          Valid forwardModel values: CS | FSlin | FS | QP",
    "alpha_range_log   list  Overrides param_grid['alpha'] with a log-spaced sweep.",
    "              or  null  Format: [min, max, n_steps]  (min and max both > 0,",
    "                        min < max, n_steps >= 2).",
    "                        Cleaner than listing individual alpha values by hand.",
    "                        null → param_grid['alpha'] is used as-is.",
    "                        Examples:",
    "                          8 steps from 0.001 to 5.0:",
    "                            \"alpha_range_log\": [0.001, 5.0, 8]",
    "                          → alpha values ≈ [0.001, 0.003, 0.009, 0.026,",
    "                                            0.074, 0.215, 0.623, 1.812, 5.0]",
    "                          Disabled:",
    "                            \"alpha_range_log\": null",
    "cond_ranges       list  Per-layer starting conductivity bounds [mS/m].",
    "                        Each element is [min, max] or [single_value].",
    "                        Length must equal number of layers (len(depths0)+1).",
    "                        Examples:",
    "                          4-layer, all with range (generates 2 starting points):",
    "                            \"cond_ranges\": [",
    "                              [5.0, 250.0],",
    "                              [5.0, 250.0],",
    "                              [10.0, 300.0],",
    "                              [10.0, 300.0]",
    "                            ]",
    "                          4-layer, pinned starting values (no EC diversity):",
    "                            \"cond_ranges\": [",
    "                              [30.0],",
    "                              [80.0],",
    "                              [120.0],",
    "                              [200.0]",
    "                            ]",
    "                          Wide bounds for maximum ensemble spread:",
    "                            \"cond_ranges\": [",
    "                              [1.0, 300.0],",
    "                              [1.0, 300.0],",
    "                              [5.0, 500.0],",
    "                              [5.0, 500.0]",
    "                            ]",
    "forward_model     str   Default EMagPy forward model for all ensemble members.",
    "                        Per-member overrides go in param_grid['forwardModel'].",
    "                        Example: \"forward_model\": \"CS\"",
    "gamma             float Temporal regularisation between time steps (>= 0).",
    "                        0.0 → no smoothing (recommended for most cases).",
    "                        0.2 → gentle smoothing across survey epochs.",
    "                        Examples:",
    "                          Off:    \"gamma\": 0.0",
    "                          Gentle: \"gamma\": 0.2",
    "                          Strong: \"gamma\": 1.0",
    "════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════",
    "SWC / TDR SENSOR NETWORK FIELDS",
    "════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════",
    "num_swc_positions int   Number of horizontal positions where SWC/TDR sensors",
    "                        are placed. Total probes = num_swc_positions × n_layers.",
    "                        Increasing this improves calibration spatial coverage",
    "                        but has diminishing RMSE returns beyond ~n_points/2.",
    "                        Default: 4.",
    "                        Examples:",
    "                          Sparse (paper default):   \"num_swc_positions\": 4",
    "                          Dense coverage:           \"num_swc_positions\": 8",
    "                          Single calibration tower: \"num_swc_positions\": 1",
    "swc_depths        list  Explicit sensor installation depths [m].",
    "              or  null  null → pipeline derives depths from layer_centers",
    "                        (midpoints of depths0 intervals).",
    "                        Use a custom list to test the effect of sensor depth",
    "                        mis-match relative to inversion layer boundaries.",
    "                        Length should equal n_layers for full coverage, but",
    "                        shorter lists are accepted (remaining layers use EC",
    "                        column mean as fallback).",
    "                        Examples:",
    "                          Auto (layer centres, recommended):",
    "                            \"swc_depths\": null",
    "                          Sensors exactly at layer centres for depths0=[0.3,0.6,1.0]:",
    "                            \"swc_depths\": [0.15, 0.45, 0.80, 1.25]",
    "                          Sensors shifted upward (tests mis-match bias):",
    "                            \"swc_depths\": [0.10, 0.35, 0.65, 1.05]",
    "window_m          float Half-width of the spatial averaging window that matches",
    "                        each TDR probe to its nearest EM measurement indices [m].",
    "                        Recommendation: start at half the instrument coil spacing.",
    "                        If [WARN] 'No EM measurement within window_m' appears,",
    "                        increase this value.",
    "                        Default: 1.0.",
    "                        Examples:",
    "                          Tight (dense EM grid):   \"window_m\": 0.5",
    "                          Standard:                \"window_m\": 1.0",
    "                          Wide (sparse EM grid):   \"window_m\": 2.0",
    "════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════",
    "OBSERVATION NOISE FIELDS",
    "════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════",
    "eca_noise_level   float Relative Gaussian noise added to synthetic ECa BEFORE",
    "                        inversion (std = eca_noise_level × ECa_signal).",
    "                        This is the PRIMARY driver of ensemble spread and the",
    "                        shape of the Fig. 3 RMSE optimisation curve.",
    "                        Use 0.03–0.05 to reproduce paper-like behaviour.",
    "                        Examples:",
    "                          Clean (no spread):       \"eca_noise_level\": 0.0",
    "                          Realistic instrument:    \"eca_noise_level\": 0.03",
    "                          Noisy field conditions:  \"eca_noise_level\": 0.05",
    "                          Extreme stress test:     \"eca_noise_level\": 0.10",
    "tdr_noise_std     float Absolute Gaussian noise added to theta_obs [m³/m³].",
    "                        Affects the RMSE floor; has less impact on spread than",
    "                        eca_noise_level.",
    "                        Examples:",
    "                          Lab-grade sensor:        \"tdr_noise_std\": 0.01",
    "                          Realistic field sensor:  \"tdr_noise_std\": 0.03",
    "                          Degraded sensor:         \"tdr_noise_std\": 0.05",
    "cache_tag         str   Optional suffix appended to the cache filename.",
    "                        Change this whenever you alter depths0 or cond_ranges",
    "                        to avoid loading a stale cached ensemble.",
    "                        Example: \"cache_tag\": \"my_scenario_v2\"",
    "description       str   Free-text label shown in pipeline log and report.",
    "                        Example: \"description\": \"Wide alpha sweep, free interfaces\"",
    "════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════",
    "HOW TO RUN SCENARIOS",
    "════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════",
    "── Basic usage ──────────────────────────────────────────────",
    "  Run the default scenario (1-D mode):",
    "    ./run_pipeline.sh",
    "  Run a named scenario:",
    "    ./run_pipeline.sh -s free_all",
    "    ./run_pipeline.sh -s mixed_middle_free",
    "    ./run_pipeline.sh -s high_ensemble_spread",
    "  Run in 2-D UTM grid mode:",
    "    ./run_pipeline.sh --mode 2d",
    "    ./run_pipeline.sh --mode 2d -s dense_swc_coverage",
    "  Run with a custom JSON scenario file:",
    "    ./run_pipeline.sh -s my_scenario -c /data/my_scenarios.json",
    "── Spatial grid size (2-D mode only) ────────────────────────",
    "  Control the number of UTM grid points with --nx and --ny.",
    "  These are ignored in 1-D mode.",
    "    ./run_pipeline.sh --mode 2d --nx 15 --ny 8",
    "    ./run_pipeline.sh --mode 2d -s free_all --nx 20 --ny 10",
    "── Calling run_pipeline.py directly (without the shell wrapper) ─────",
    "  python run_pipeline.py --scenario default",
    "  python run_pipeline.py --scenario free_all --mode 2d",
    "  python run_pipeline.py --scenario fine_layers_fixed --config /data/my.json",
    "── Scenario discovery & validation ───────────────────────────────",
    "  List all available scenarios:",
    "    ./run_pipeline.sh --list",
    "    python scenario_loader.py --list",
    "  Validate every scenario in the JSON (catches schema errors before running):",
    "    ./run_pipeline.sh --validate",
    "    python -c \"from scenario_loader import validate_all; validate_all()\"",
    "  Inspect a single scenario's resolved config:",
    "    python scenario_loader.py mixed_middle_free",
    "    python scenario_loader.py high_ensemble_spread",
    "── Common scenario combinations and what to expect ───────────────────────",
    "  Quick smoke-test (1 ensemble member, fast):",
    "    ./run_pipeline.sh -s default",
    "    → 1 member, fixed depths, clean data. RMSE curve is flat (no spread).",
    "      Useful to verify the pipeline runs end-to-end.",
    "  Realistic paper-like run (moderate spread, clear U-curve):",
    "    ./run_pipeline.sh -s fixed_dense",
    "    → 8 members (2α × 2method × 2model), fixed depths, eca_noise=0.03.",
    "      Expect a clear minimum in the Fig. 3 RMSE curve around K=4–6.",
    "  Maximum ensemble spread (widest RMSE optimisation curve):",
    "    ./run_pipeline.sh -s high_ensemble_spread",
    "    → alpha log-swept [0.001–5.0] × 3 forward models × 2 methods.",
    "      Best scenario for demonstrating the ensemble benefit.",
    "  Free interfaces (geometry uncertainty):",
    "    ./run_pipeline.sh -s geometric_uncertainty",
    "    → Interfaces float during inversion. Expect wider CV maps and",
    "      depth-spread visible in the Step 1 ensemble plot.",
    "  Noisy field conditions stress test:",
    "    ./run_pipeline.sh -s noisy_sensors",
    "    → 5% TDR noise + 10% ECa noise. RMSE floor will be higher.",
    "      Tests ensemble robustness under degraded data quality.",
    "  Dense SWC coverage (8 sensor positions):",
    "    ./run_pipeline.sh -s dense_swc_coverage",
    "    → More calibration points per inversion. Compare final RMSE",
    "      against 'default' (4 positions) to quantify sensor density benefit.",
    "  Sensor depth mis-match experiment:",
    "    ./run_pipeline.sh -s custom_swc_depths",
    "    → Sensors placed off layer centres. Introduces a systematic bias",
    "      in the Waxman-Smits calibration; useful for sensitivity analysis.",
    "  Time-lapse with temporal smoothing, 2-D grid:",
    "    ./run_pipeline.sh -s free_timelapse_smooth --mode 2d --nx 12 --ny 6",
    "    → Produces XZ cross-sections AND XY plan-view water-content maps.",
    "── Full argument reference (run_pipeline.sh) ────────────────────",
    "  -s / --scenario NAME    Scenario key from this JSON file",
    "  -c / --config   PATH    Path to a custom JSON scenario file",
    "       --mode     1d|2d   Spatial mode (default: 1d)",
    "       --nx       INT     Grid columns in 2-D mode (default: 10)",
    "       --ny       INT     Grid rows    in 2-D mode (default: 5)",
    "       --list             Print scenario names and exit",
    "       --validate         Validate all scenarios and exit",
    "  -h / --help             Show shell usage message"
  ],
